SEEDLESS WALLET TRANSITION


Your wallet. Without the phrase.

Starting Q1 2027, Ledger is retiring the 24-word Secret Recovery Phrase. Al=
l devices move to a fully seedless architecture. Private keys are generated=
, stored, and signed entirely inside the secure element. The key never leav=
es the chip.

No phrase to write down. No paper backup to lose. No 24 words for an attack=
er to extract. The secure element handles everything. The same CC EAL6+ chi=
p that protects your keys today now owns the full lifecycle.

WHAT=E2=80=99S CHANGING

=E2=80=A2	 Seed phrase generation and display are removed from Ledger Walle=
t and all device firmware.	=20
=E2=80=A2	 Key generation, storage, and signing stay inside the CC EAL6+ se=
cure element. The key is born on the chip and dies on the chip. Zero exposu=
re.	=20
=E2=80=A2	 Recovery runs through the secure element. Lose your device, buy =
a new one, authenticate; funds restored. No phrase needed.	=20
=E2=80=A2	 Existing seed-phrase wallets keep working. You will migrate fund=
s to a seedless wallet through Ledger Wallet once the firmware ships.	=20
